            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, I can not reproduce. First, the reproduction steps most certainly need some custom value of 'signcolumn'. For example, `vim.o.signcolumn = 'yes:2'`. But even with that I can not reproduce.\r\n\r\nWould you mind narrowing down reproduction steps to minimal setup. Ideally, if it uses only 'mini.diff' as a source of signs and only necessary options set. For example, [with these lines as starting point](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/c78332b4c71ad3c2a09efe6acd0a51283627258f/scripts/init-deps-example.lua#L1-L17)?\r\n\r\nIf this happens only on the first line, I have an idea of why this happens, but I can not reliably fix it without reproducing it and writing test for it.",
